From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv64: skip the libgfortran RPATH fixup when there is none

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [this build's riscv64 gfortran links libgfortran statically into libscipy_openblas.so instead of as a separate shared object, unlike x86_64/aarch64]

Every leg that gets past the OpenBLAS compile fails here on real riscv64
CI (PR #4888), identically on manylinux and musllinux:

    + unzip dist/scipy_openblas32-...-riscv64.whl '*libgfortran*'
    caution: filename not matched:  *libgfortran*
    ##[error]Process completed with exit code 11.

auditwheel repair's own log for the same run never mentions copying or
grafting any shared library at all (confirmed from the real job log),
so this isn't a glob/naming mismatch: the wheel genuinely has no
separate libgfortran*.so to RPATH-fix on this build - unlike the
upstream-published x86_64 wheel for this exact version, which does
bundle one (its real PyPI wheel carries
scipy_openblas32/lib/libgfortran-040039e1.so.5.0.0). GPL-source
availability for gcc-gfortran is unaffected either way: this repo's
own gpl_sources job already collects it from the same manylinux image
regardless of how libgfortran ends up linked.

Guard on the wheel's own contents rather than $PLAT, so the fix holds
for any future target with the same static-gfortran behavior instead
of enumerating riscv64 by name.
---
 tools/build_wheel.sh | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/build_wheel.sh b/tools/build_wheel.sh
index f2f2ca9..c374d9f 100644
--- a/tools/build_wheel.sh
+++ b/tools/build_wheel.sh
@@ -85,14 +85,16 @@ else
     rm dist/scipy_openblas*-none-any.whl
     # Add an RPATH to libgfortran:
     # https://github.com/pypa/auditwheel/issues/451
-    if [ "$MB_ML_LIBC" == "musllinux" ]; then
-      apk add zip
-    else
-      yum install -y zip
+    if unzip -l dist/*.whl | grep -q libgfortran; then
+      if [ "$MB_ML_LIBC" == "musllinux" ]; then
+        apk add zip
+      else
+        yum install -y zip
+      fi
+      unzip dist/*.whl "*libgfortran*"
+      patchelf --force-rpath --set-rpath '$ORIGIN' */lib/libgfortran*
+      zip dist/*.whl */lib/libgfortran*
     fi
-    unzip dist/*.whl "*libgfortran*"
-    patchelf --force-rpath --set-rpath '$ORIGIN' */lib/libgfortran*
-    zip dist/*.whl */lib/libgfortran*
 fi
 
 if [ "${PLAT}" == "arm64" ]; then
